    4. For each small object, generate a random 4-connected polyomino with area in [1,3].
    5. Place objects one by one on the black grid, ensuring no two share a 4-connected neighbor (they must remain distinct 4-connected components). Diagonal adjacency is allowed.
    6. If a placement fails after reasonable retries, shrink remaining objects or retry from step 1.
    7. Verify total red density is 10-40% and both small and large categories are non-empty.
